20-free-markers: curry.free on the expression route.

Seam: a curry.free() marker is one Curry variable; a binding is private to
the evaluation that made it; a typed marker; the anonymous variable of the
text route.  (The name wart of curry.free, P7, is shown by 34.)
Sources: memo A11; catalogue P21, P24, P42; Using the API, "Expression
Modifiers".  Backends: py, cxx.  Oracle: oracle.out, the PAKCS 3.4.1 REPL on
the same goals as text with "where x free".

Expected output: (x =:= 1, x, x) gives (True, 1, 1), one marker bound once
and read twice; the same marker bound to 2 in a second goal, and free again
afterwards, printed as _a.  A marker types as a; with exprtype='[Int]' as
[Int].  A free Char inside a String prints as [_a];
under the converter the join of the characters meets a node and a plain
TypeError escapes (P21), the same on both backends.  On the text route
"_ ++ [x] =:= [1,2,3] where x free" gives {x=3} True, and the anonymous
variable is not reported.  PAKCS prints the typed marker [x] :: String as
{x=x} [x], where Sprite prints [_a].  Pins no defect.
